    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's a bit too short. can you expand on the punctuality part? i need to explain *why* it matters to the rest of the team so it doesn't just sound like i'm nitpicking. like, how does being late affect the team dynamic and the workflow? make it sound more substantial.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right, adding context makes the feedback much stronger. You can expand by explaining that the stand-up is crucial for setting the daily rhythm, which is vital for coordinated workflow. For example, late arrivals can disrupt the momentum, making it difficult for the team to get an immediate pulse on priorities. I suggest framing it as an impact on team efficiency, not just a personal rule.\n\nHere is a more substantial draft incorporating that idea:\n\n\"[Name] has demonstrated exceptional skill in managing our key accounts, consistently exceeding expectations in client retention and satisfaction. Their dedication to nurturing these large partnerships is truly commendable. To maintain this high level of performance, we need to ensure consistent alignment across the team, which requires punctuality for our morning stand-ups. These brief meetings are the backbone of our daily coordination; when team members arrive late, it disrupts the established workflow and delays the critical synchronization needed for the entire team to hit the ground running. I want to partner with you to address this so that your excellent client work is supported by seamless team operations.\"",
      "source": "target",
